        "orario": "17:51",
        "timestamp": 1774972275,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. EU shows support to Ukraine at Bucha commemoration Europe Issued on: 31/03/2026 - 17:51 Modified: 31/03/2026 - 17:52 Four years on from the Bucha massacre, the Ukrainian town is remembering its dead. Russian military forces retreated from Bucha in 2022, hundreds of bodies were discovered, including women, children and elderly people, many of the corpses had been left lying in the streets. A delegation of EU foreign ministers arrived in Kyiv on March 31 to mark the anniversary and discuss ways to further support Ukraine. As Ukraine commemorates the Bucha massacre, Russia rejects idea of Easter truce 31/03/2026 Europe Bucha massacre 'part of deliberate campaign to pave a road of destruction to Kyiv' 31/03/2026 Europe EU ministers in Kyiv to look at justice for crimes committed in Bucha 31/03/2026 Europe EU ministers commemorate Bucha massacre and reaffirm support to Ukraine 31/03/2026 Europe Ukraine's Bucha commemorates four years since massacre 31/03/2026 Europe Police arrest two more over attempted attack on US bank HQ in Paris 30/03/2026 Europe Paintings by Renoir, Cézanne and Matisse stolen from Italian museum 30/03/2026 Europe Ukraine signs defence agreements with Gulf Nations eager to fend off Iranian drones 30/03/2026 Middle East Russian strikes on Ukraine kill at least 5 28/03/2026 Europe"
